<title>USA: Retail sales solid, but Gymboree flounders.</title>
<headline>Retail sales solid, but Gymboree flounders.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most retailers enjoyed solid November sales heading into the all-important holiday selling season, but comparisons were difficult because the Thanksgiving Day holiday was a week later in 1996.</p>
<p>Gymboree Corp was a notable exception on the downside, off 6-3/4 to 21. Gymboree reported that November same-store sales slumped 15 percent.</p>
<p>Both Morgan Stanley and Alex Brown downgraded the stock.</p>
</text>
